title: Constitutional Court rules on the Catalan Cybersecurity Agency
face-image: img/events/constitucional.jpg
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: constitutional_digital_trigger
max-visits: 1
role: event
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.parlament_digital_variant == "national_scope") {
        G.deactivateLaw(Q, "digital_agency_national_scope", "struck_down");
        Q.cybersecurity_agency_scope = "generalitat";
    }
    Q.cat_spa_relations -= 5;
!}

= Constitutional Court rules on the Catalan Cybersecurity Agency

[? if parlament_digital_variant == "public_services": The Constitutional Court has ruled in favour of the Catalan Cybersecurity Agency. It has deemed the protection of Catalonia's public administration to fall within the Generalitat's powers, while expecting the agency to cooperate with other law-enforcement bodies. ?]

[? if parlament_digital_variant == "national_scope": The Constitutional Court has ruled in favour of greatly reducing the agency's powers. While the agency itself survives with a limited role in protecting public services and resources, its authority over the Catalan citizens and companies has been reduced to basically zero.?]

- @digital_ruling_safe: Unexpected, but nice!
- @digital_ruling_accept: The Generalitat accepts the ruling
- @digital_ruling_protest: The Generalitat condemns the ruling!

@digital_ruling_safe
view-if: parlament_digital_variant == "public_services"
go-to: post_event

@digital_ruling_accept
view-if: parlament_digital_variant == "national_scope"
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.cat_spa_relations += 2;
    Q.independence_trust -= 5;
!}

The Generalitat will, for now, comply and concentrate resources on its own systems and services. The agency remains useful, but it has lost much of its intended role.

- @post_event: Continue...

@digital_ruling_protest
view-if: parlament_digital_variant == "national_scope"
choose-if: (player_party == "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party == "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting))
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have the capacity to influence the Generalitat's response to this law
on-arrival: {!
    Q.cat_spa_relations -= 2;
!}

[? if president_gender = "m": President ?][? if president_gender = "f": Presidenta ?][+ president +] has stepped forward to denounce the ruling as an unnecessarily restrictive reading of Catalan self-government. This will hardly change the ruling as the agency's powers are stripped down, but the Generalitat has bowed to push the agency's role to the very maximum.

- @post_event: Continue...
